# build outputs
target/
build/
dist/
*.apk
*.aab

# android / gradle
.gradle/
local.properties
.cxx/

# apple
*.xcuserdatad
DerivedData/

# node (web shell tooling)
node_modules/

# env scratch
/tmp/
# Where env/ scripts stage things they build: the emulator dlopen probe (and,
# until D3.4, the iroh-ffi clone). Reproducible from the scripts, so never committed.
/.build/
mutants.out/

# The croft-ffi native library, as `env/build-croft-ffi-android.sh` installs it
# into the SOCIAL module (S1 moved it there — the calling app must not carry a
# library nothing in it calls).
#
# Still untracked, and now for a better reason than in S0: it is a 2MB build
# output of code in this same repo, reproducible with one command, and a binary
# in git is a binary nobody reviews. `make ffi-android` regenerates it.
# (`libiroh_ffi.so` WAS committed because its source was not here; D3.4 removed
# it — the calling app's iroh is ours now.)
android/social/src/main/jniLibs/*/libcroft_ffi.so
# D3: the calling app carries it too, for the same reason and with the same
# regeneration command.
android/app/src/main/jniLibs/*/libcroft_ffi.so

# The apple shell's generated uniffi bindings (env/gen-swift-bindings.sh
# writes them from the built cdylib) and SwiftPM's build directory.
shell/apple/Sources/croft_ffiFFI/include/
shell/apple/Sources/CroftFFI/Generated/
shell/apple/.generated/
shell/apple/.build/
